  "title": "Sebi Proposes Raising ISIN Cap and Easing Debt Listing Norms",
  "summary": "Sebi has proposed raising the annual ISIN limit for private debt securities from 14 to 17 to ease funding constraints and reduce refinancing risks. Additionally, it aims to scrap mandatory listing of past debt issues to streamline the process. A data breach at Framework Platforms and a fraud case against former Southern Water employees have also emerged, highlighting concerns about cybersecurity and environmental accountability.",
