      "title": "Sebi keeps Inox Clean Energy's IPO papers to raise ₹10K cr in abeyance",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/news/sebi-keeps-inox-clean-energy-s-ipo-papers-to-raise-10k-cr-in-abeyance-126100101123_1.html",
      "description": "Markets regulator Sebi has kept in 'abeyance' the draft offer documents of Inox Clean Energy Ltd, which is looking to raise up to Rs 10,000 crore through an initial public offering (IPO).\nThe proposed IPO comprises a fresh issue of equity shares worth up to Rs 8,000 crore and an offer-for-sale (OFS) of shares, amounting to Rs 2,000 crore by promoter Devansh Jain, according to the draft red herring prospectus (DRHP).\nThe status of the issue was updated by the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Sebi) on Thursday under the list of IPOs whose observations have been kept in abeyance.\nThe company had filed its draft papers with the regulator on September 29.\nWithout specifying reasons, the regulator stated that the \"issuance of observations (has been) kept in abeyance\", according to an update on its website.\nThe proposed issue could rank among the largest IPOs in India's private-sector renewable energy space.\nInox Clean Energy, part of the INOXGFL Group, proposes to use the procee",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-01T13:59:21"
    },
